**Discrepancy with the paper.** The paper's tight lower bound
$\underline y-\overline x+J(\overline y)J'(\overline y)
-(2Q_\beta(\frac{\underline x+\overline y}2)-Q_\beta(\underline x))
Q_\beta'(\frac{\underline x+\underline y}2)$ relies on item 2 ("$2Q_\beta(\frac{x+y}2)-Q_\beta(x)$
increasing in $y$") and on $Q'_\beta(\frac{x+y}2)\ge0$, which fail where $x+y>1$. Lean: the factor
